        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s093-u001",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குமுதா",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s093-d001",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 111,
            "printedPage": 103
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chinnamma! Chinnamma!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s093-u002",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s093-d002",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 111,
            "printedPage": 103
          }
        ],
        "text": "Don't cry, Kumudha!...",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s093-u003",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பாண்டியன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s093-d003",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 111,
            "printedPage": 103
          }
        ],
        "text": "You did not kill your younger brother! His own past deeds took revenge upon him!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s093-u004",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s093-d004",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 111,
            "printedPage": 103
          }
        ],
        "text": "If he had been a good man from the beginning, why would I ever have become angry with him? Why would I kill, while he writhed, the treasure I had so tenderly raised?",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s093-u005",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குமுதா",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s093-d005",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 111,
            "printedPage": 103
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chinnamma!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s093-u006",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s093-d006",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 112,
            "printedPage": 104
          }
        ],
        "text": "Kumudha! Your uncle received the fitting reward for the suffering he caused you and the people of the town! And by doing this deed, I too showed that I—the woman you once suspected—was without stain!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s093-u007",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குமுதா",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s093-d007",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 112,
            "printedPage": 104
          }
        ],
        "text": "Forgive me, Chinnamma!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s093-u008",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s093-d008",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 112,
            "printedPage": 104
          }
        ],
        "text": "Don't cry, my dear, don't cry! All right, it is time. Kumudha! Pandiyan! I am going.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s093-u009",
        "kind": "stage-direction",
        "speakerLabel": null,
        "sourceRecordId": null,
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 112,
            "printedPage": 104
          }
        ],
        "text": "(There are tears in the eyes of the female students. Poomaalai sees them.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s093-u010",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s093-d009",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 112,
            "printedPage": 104
          }
        ],
        "text": "Kumudha! Fulfil my one request! (Pointing to the female students.) Here are the flower-clusters of a new world! Labour to kindle the lamp of knowledge in these young hearts. You and Pandiyan must strive to make the counsel 'Look Back' a counsel needed by everyone—those who live well, those who lie in distress, and those engaged in destructive deeds! I am going. (To the female students.) My lovely little birds! Blessings to all of you! Do not forget the teaching 'Look Back.' I am going to a place from which I will not return.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s093-u011",
        "kind": "stage-direction",
        "speakerLabel": null,
        "sourceRecordId": null,
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 112,
            "printedPage": 104
          }
        ],
        "text": "(The children stand in tears. The warders lead Poomaalai away.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s093-u012",
        "kind": "written-text",
        "speakerLabel": null,
        "sourceRecordId": null,
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 112,
            "printedPage": 104
          }
        ],
        "text": "Vanakkam.",
        "notes": [
          "The final printed word 'வணக்கம்.' is preserved as a closing salutation. The following star is structural and is not turned into a translation unit."
        ]
      }
